Two universes $\mathcal{U}_1$ and $\mathcal{U}_2$ are considered
equivalent if they differ only by a relabeling of structural coordinates:


\[
\mathcal{U}_1 \sim \mathcal{U}_2
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
\exists \;\Phi \text{ invertible such that }
\Phi(G_1) = G_2.
