\[
\text{sens}(\pi) = 
\sup_{x \in \mathcal{S}}
\left\|
\frac{\partial \pi(x)}{\partial x}
\right\|.
\]


High sensitivity indicates that small structural changes may produce
large variations in projected phenomena.

\subsection{Implications of Structural Closure}
Once the generative system is closed, all admissible structures are
finite expressions over the golden basis. This implies:


\[
\text{No new invariants can arise.}
\]
